D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program
S: Symbol Table List

  SYMBOLS:

BLOCK AT LINE 1, AUTO STORAGE 0 BYTES
a 0000 E46L13 ENTRY PARAMETERS(0) EXTERNAL CONSTANT
BLOCK AT LINE 7, AUTO STORAGE 20 BYTES
c 0000 OUTF FILE EXTERNAL STATIC
c 0000 C CHAR(20) AUTOMATIC
   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46L13

   1 a 0000 E46L13:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2a] runtime 2: CHARACTER FIXED.  `c = 42' leaves 19 characters of the declared
   4 a 0006      20 UNASSIGNED, and NOTHING in this project has ever measured what DR's runtime writes
   5 a 0006      into those -- blanks, NULs, or the cell's prior bytes.  That is the question this object
   6 a 0006      asks, and the answer is read out of DR's own file, not guessed. */
   7 c 0006   dcl outf file, c char(20);
   8 c 0006   c = 'ABC';
   9 c 0013   open file(outf) stream output title('L13OUT DAT');
  10 c 0030   put file(outf) list(c);
  11 c 004A   close file(outf);
  12 c 0050   put list('DONE');
  13 c 0067   stop;
  14 a 006A end E46L13;

CODE SIZE = 006A
DATA AREA = 0025
FREE SYMS = 386F
END  COMPILATION
